  "note": "Independent re-judgment against RFC 4271 Section 5.1.4 ('If a BGP speaker is configured to alter the value of the MULTI_EXIT_DISC attribute received over EBGP, then altering the value MUST be done prior to determining the degree of preference of the route and prior to performing route selection (Decision Process phases 1 and 2).') after RFC 8893 edit to Reactor.evaluateLibraryChain (filter_library.go). Inspected git diff: evaluateLibraryChain adds a single field propagation line copying SkipRPKIValidation and JudgeRPKIValidation from libraryIntentContext onto policychain.ExternalRoute. On the ingress rail (runIngressPolicyChainMeta), both flags are always false, so ingress chain evaluation, MED rewrite via rewriteLibrary/buildModifiedPayload/filter_delta_handlers.go, and pre-decision-process ordering are completely unchanged. Both tagged tests (TestRFC4271ReceivedMEDAlteredBeforeTheDecisionProcess and TestRFC4271MEDAlterationHappensAtIngress) are unchanged and PASS (go test -tags ze_bgp ./internal/component/bgp/reactor). All 23 existing code bindings (including bare filter_delta_handlers.go) and prior discrimination provenance remain valid; the enforced verdict stands.",
